<main class="app" data-locations-url="<%= locations_path(format: :json) %>">
  <div class="map" id="map" role="region" aria-label="Map of Ruby companies, meetups and events"></div>

  <aside class="panel" id="panel" aria-label="Places">
    <header class="panel__head">
      <a class="brand" href="/">
        <svg class="brand__mark" viewBox="0 0 32 32" aria-hidden="true">
          <path class="brand__pin" d="M16 2c-6.1 0-11 4.8-11 10.8C5 20.6 16 30 16 30s11-9.4 11-17.2C27 6.8 22.1 2 16 2Z"/>
          <path class="brand__gem" d="m11.5 11.2 2.2-2.9h4.6l2.2 2.9L16 17.6Z"/>
        </svg>
        <span class="brand__name">Ruby Map</span>
      </a>

      <div class="panel__tools">
        <button type="button" class="icon-button" id="theme-toggle" aria-label="Theme: system" title="Theme: system">
          <svg class="icon icon--system" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="8"/><path d="M12 4a8 8 0 0 1 0 16Z" class="icon__fill"/></svg>
          <svg class="icon icon--light" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="4"/><path d="M12 2v2M12 20v2M4.9 4.9l1.4 1.4M17.7 17.7l1.4 1.4M2 12h2M20 12h2M4.9 19.1l1.4-1.4M17.7 6.3l1.4-1.4"/></svg>
          <svg class="icon icon--dark" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 14.5A8 8 0 1 1 9.5 4a6.5 6.5 0 0 0 10.5 10.5Z"/></svg>
        </button>
        <button type="button" class="icon-button" commandfor="about" command="show-modal" aria-label="About Ruby Map" title="About Ruby Map">
          <svg class="icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"/><path d="M12 11v5M12 8h.01"/></svg>
        </button>
      </div>
    </header>

    <p class="panel__summary" id="summary">Ruby companies, meetups and events around the world.</p>

    <div class="panel__controls">
      <label class="search">
        <svg class="icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="11" cy="11" r="7"/><path d="m20 20-4-4"/></svg>
        <span class="visually-hidden">Search by name or place</span>
        <input type="search" id="search" placeholder="Search by name or place" autocomplete="off" spellcheck="false">
      </label>

      <fieldset class="filters" id="filters">
        <legend class="visually-hidden">Show</legend>
        <label class="filter"><input type="radio" name="type" value="all" checked><span><em>All</em><b data-count="all">&nbsp;</b></span></label>
        <label class="filter filter--business"><input type="radio" name="type" value="business"><span><em>Companies</em><b data-count="business">&nbsp;</b></span></label>
        <label class="filter filter--meetup"><input type="radio" name="type" value="meetup"><span><em>Meetups</em><b data-count="meetup">&nbsp;</b></span></label>
        <label class="filter filter--event"><input type="radio" name="type" value="event"><span><em>Events</em><b data-count="event">&nbsp;</b></span></label>
      </fieldset>
    </div>

    <div class="panel__listhead">
      <h2 class="section-heading" id="list-heading">Places</h2>
      <label class="checkbox">
        <input type="checkbox" id="in-view">
        <span>Only on the map</span>
      </label>
    </div>

    <ol class="places" id="places" aria-labelledby="list-heading"></ol>
    <p class="places__empty" id="places-empty" hidden></p>

    <button type="button" class="panel__toggle" id="panel-toggle" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="panel">
      <span class="panel__toggle-show">Show list</span>
      <span class="panel__toggle-hide">Show map</span>
    </button>
  </aside>

  <dialog class="about" id="about" aria-labelledby="about-title" closedby="any">
    <header class="about__head">
      <h2 id="about-title">About Ruby Map</h2>
      <button type="button" class="icon-button" commandfor="about" command="close" aria-label="Close">
        <svg class="icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M6 6l12 12M18 6 6 18"/></svg>
      </button>
    </header>
    <p>Whilst travelling to other cities I've often wondered: "What's going on in the local <a href="https://www.ruby-lang.org/en/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Ruby</a> community?"</p>
    <p>To answer this question, hopefully fellow Rubyists will <a href="https://github.com/lewispb/rubymap/blob/master/data/seeds/organizations.yml" target="_blank" rel="noopener">share their organization, meetup or event</a> and anyone interested will be able to discover the Ruby world around them.</p>
    <p>Sometimes folks are interested in finding a new gig, in a new location. Ruby Map might be useful for that too, if companies share that they are hiring.</p>
    <p>Any questions? Contact me, <a href="https://twitter.com/lewispb" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Lewis</a>.</p>
    <p class="about__credits">Many meetups and events, with their images, come from <a href="https://www.rubyevents.org" target="_blank" rel="noopener">RubyEvents.org</a>, the community-maintained directory of Ruby events. Company photos and logos come from each company's own website. Descriptions are written by AI from that text. Map data © <a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright" target="_blank" rel="noopener">OpenStreetMap contributors</a>. Tiles by <a href="https://openfreemap.org" target="_blank" rel="noopener">OpenFreeMap</a>. Rendered with <a href="https://maplibre.org" target="_blank" rel="noopener">MapLibre</a>.</p>
  </dialog>
</main>
